      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Getting Started with NexusCore\n\nTo begin using NexusCore effectively, you must first secure your access and understand the request lifecycle. Authentication is mandatory for all operations and relies on a strict standard based on our latest security protocols.\n\n## 1. Authentication Setup\n\nEvery API call requires a valid token. Username and password methods are deprecated; please use the OAuth2 flow or direct API key injection for production.\n\n*   Retrieve your unique `API_KEY` from the Nexus Dashboard > Credentials section.\n*   Initialize a secure client session ensuring headers are set before any network handshake occurs.\n*   Rotate keys every 90 days to maintain compliance with enterprise security standards.\n*   Enable strict Bearer token validation in your local development environment (`NODE_ENV=production`).\n\n## 2. Making Your First Request\n\nOnce authenticated, you can interact with the Core nodes using standard RESTful patterns. The library handles handshake latency transparently for standard GET operations.\n\n*   Initialize the client with your region-specific endpoint URL (e.g., `us-east-1`).\n*   Call `client.auth.list()` to retrieve your current permissions and role assignments.\n*   Parse the JSON response asynchronously using the provided `.then()` chain to",
